node_modules/
coverage/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Output of every `browser-inspector` run: screenshots, report.json, session journals — the page
# under test is somebody's application and what lands here is its data.
.scribe-devtools/

# Output of every `nx-angular-inspector` run: digests of somebody's workspace. Short on purpose —
# the path is printed on every line of stdout, and `.ws/projects.md` is 3 o200k tokens against 10
# for the long form (measured back when this repository still had a tokenizer). Its twin is the
# `!.ws/**` entry in biome.jsonc: one run of the tool would otherwise turn `biome format .` red.
.ws/

# `npm run portable` output. On this branch it is an on-demand build, not a tracked release
# artifact — nothing here is committed.
download/

# A read config carries the URLs, selectors and flows of the app it inspects — yours, not the
# tool's.
read.config.*.json

# A live MCP config would put thousands of tokens of tool schemas into every agent request — not
# paying that is the point of this repository. Nothing here ships one; a copy made for a manual
# comparison must not be committed either (twin of the rule on `main`).
.mcp.json
.vscode/mcp.json

# copilot-builder/ is a TEMPLATE tree: its .vscode/mcp.json is content, not a live client config
# (one stdio server, `ng mcp`, owned by a single hidden subagent) — the rule above is for this root.
!copilot-builder/.vscode/mcp.json
